            "reason": "semicolon",
            "scope": "grid_storage.body",
            "text": "Operating storage now has a weighted average duration of 2.8 hours, and 45.7% of capacity has at least four hours of duration; both measures improved slightly. The active interconnection queue remains 2,061 GW, but only 24.2% is in executed-agreement or construction stages. Utility Dive reported that FERC approved a MISO plan to speed its legacy interconnection study process. The change addresses processing, but it does not by itself move the large early-stage queue into construction."
