            "message": "Semicolon present; review for clause stacking.",
            "reason": "semicolon",
            "scope": "macro.paragraphs[1]",
            "text": "The electricity system continues to separate announced scale from delivered capacity. Commercial demand is growing 3.5%, compared with 1.8% for total retail demand, and retail prices are up 5.1%. Net planned generation additions total 227.1 GW, while the active interconnection queue stands at 2,061 GW; only 24.2% of queued capacity has reached executed-agreement or construction stages. Utility Dive reported TVA\u2019s $1.7 billion data-center deal under a new large-load tariff. The deal makes large-load contracting more concrete, but it does not convert the wider generation and interconnection pipelines into operating capacity."
          },
