            "reason": "semicolon",
            "scope": "macro.paragraphs[2]",
            "text": "Broader outcomes remain mixed. Nonfarm-business productivity grew 2.1% and real output 2.3%, while real hourly compensation rose 0.6%; those aggregates are positive but do not isolate an AI contribution. The market signal is also split: the AI Equity Index edged up to 33.4, but the share of covered companies with positive one-year returns slipped to 59.3% and the median return fell materially to 7.3%. The current evidence is clearer on investment and physical expansion than on a broad economic or market payoff."
